/-!
# M₂₄ Cartan obstruction words

A cyclic Cartan witness of order seven or fifteen forces its permuting Sylow
extension to have order 7168, 15360 or 21504. For each of the 510 certified
native Sylow double cosets, a short positive word either has a forbidden
prime cycle or has the wrong cubic fixed-point type. Only the displayed
exceptional representatives survive. All finite certificates are checked
by the kernel; the generating search is not trusted.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, Definition E.3.37 and Table 7.3.4,
printed pp.239 and 699. This supplies the native M₂₄ exclusion directly.
-/

